## Summary

`Section` puts the heading column and the actions row side by side in one header row (`registry/patterns/section.rhai`). The heading column has `flex_grow().min_width(px(0))`, the actions row keeps its full width and the header does not wrap, so in a narrow container a few actions squeeze the title into a sliver and it breaks into many short lines.

Found in oh-my-byted's detail panes (about 350px wide) with a status badge, a tag and an "open in browser" button as section actions.

## How to reproduce

1. Check out `feat/design-system-0.2` (2c5e8a0).
2. Save the test below as `tests/native-keyboard/tests/section_actions_squeeze.rs`.
3. Run:
   ```
   cargo test --manifest-path tests/native-keyboard/Cargo.toml --test section_actions_squeeze -- --nocapture
   ```

The reporter's local copy is at `~/.cache/gpui-rhai-2c5e8a0/tests/native-keyboard/tests/section_actions_squeeze.rs`.

Result on 2c5e8a0: `title_keeps_room_next_to_actions` fails: in a 347px container the title "oec.affiliate.task_engine" is `29x216` (9 lines of 24px) with the actions still beside it. The control `title_without_actions_is_one_line` passes (339x24).

## Suggested fix (for the maintainers to decide)

For example: let the header wrap so the actions move below the title when they do not fit; or give the heading a minimum width (about a line of the label) before the actions are placed beside it.

