## Summary

A long `Alert` title and a long `InlineState` error title do not wrap when the container is narrower than the text. The text sits in a flex item with the default `min-width: auto`, so the item cannot shrink below the unwrapped line; the line runs past the container and is clipped.

- Alert: the title is inside `column(body)` (part `body`, `flex_grow()`, no `min_width(0)`) inside the root row.
- InlineState error: the title is inside `row([lamp, title])` inside a column with `items_start()`. Here the caller cannot fix it: `part_styles: #{ title: style().min_width(px(0)) }` still measures one long line, because the `row([lamp, title])` wrapper is not a part.
- The same happens to InlineState's stale description and refreshing title (not covered by the test).

Found in oh-my-byted's docked tools, which are often 300 to 400px wide.

## How to reproduce

1. Check out `feat/design-system-0.2` (2c5e8a0).
2. Save the test below as `tests/native-keyboard/tests/long_text_wrap.rs`.
3. Run:
   ```
   cargo test --manifest-path tests/native-keyboard/Cargo.toml --test long_text_wrap -- --nocapture
   ```

The reporter's local copy is at `~/.cache/gpui-rhai-2c5e8a0/tests/native-keyboard/tests/long_text_wrap.rs`.

Result on 2c5e8a0: `alert_title_wraps_in_a_narrow_box` fails (title `(35, 12, 513, 22)`: one 513px line in a 300px box) and `inline_state_error_title_wraps_in_a_narrow_box` fails (`(26, 12, 513, 22)`). Controls pass: Alert with `min_width(px(0))` on title / body / description wraps (253 wide, 66 high); the same text as InlineState's error `description` wraps (276 wide, 44 high). Widths depend on the test fonts.

## Suggested fix (for the maintainers to decide)

Give the flex items that hold text `min_width(px(0))` in Alert (body, title, description) and in InlineState (the lamp + title row and its children, the stale / refreshing text), so long text wraps by default.

