## Summary

`InlineState` accepts `detail` in every state (the schema has no per-state rule), but `render_InlineState` only draws it when `state == "error"` (`registry/patterns/inline_state.rhai`: `if detail != () && state == "error"`). In the stale and refreshing branches the text is silently dropped.

Stale is exactly where a caller has a raw error to show: the data is still on screen and the refresh failed. Found while moving oh-my-byted's panels to InlineState: 8 of its 0.2 widgets pass the refresh error as `detail` to a stale InlineState, and none of them shows it.

## How to reproduce

1. Check out `feat/design-system-0.2` (2c5e8a0).
